      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM with minor suggestions** — See inline comments for optional improvements. [[trajectory](go/traj/f73658fc-375b-4aae-a5d8-d33786f87b89)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality \u0026 Security:**\n- The CL successfully resolves all heap buffer overflow and over-read vulnerabilities by fully delegating memory allocation and reallocation boundaries to Zephyr\u0027s native `k_heap_calloc` and `k_heap_realloc` functions. This securely handles `count * size` multiplication and safely bounds memory copies during reallocation.\n- `plat_calloc` and `plat_realloc` are cleanly implemented as wrappers around the new safe allocators.\n- `sys_free` and `sys_alloc_usable_size` correctly handle `NULL` pointers, improving the robustness of the PAL API.\n\n**Style \u0026 Consistency:**\n- The code changes are concise, idiomatic, and adhere perfectly to Zephyr\u0027s coding guidelines.\n- The use of `COND_CODE_1(CONFIG_ZTEST, (), (static))` remains a clean way to expose internal functions to the test suite without polluting the global namespace.\n\n**Testing:**\n- The `ztest` suite provides rigorous and comprehensive coverage of the new allocator logic.\n- Using `ztest_set_fault_valid(true)` to ensure that intentional zero-sized allocations, integer overflows, and OOM conditions successfully trigger fatal panics (`k_oops()`) is an excellent defensive testing strategy.\n- Memory shrinking and growing behaviors for `realloc` are thoroughly verified.\n\nTAG\u003dagy\nCONV\u003df73658fc-375b-4aae-a5d8-d33786f87b89",
